  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "JJ has an array AAA of length NNN and an integer XXX. JJ can perform the following operation **at most once**:\n\n\nSelect a subsequence of AAA and add XXX to all the elements of that subsequence.\nFor example, if A=[2,1,6,3,5]A = [2, 1, 6, 3, 5]A=[2,1,6,3,5] and X=7X = 7X=7, we can select the subsequence [2,3,5][2, 3, 5][2,3,5] and add XXX to all the elements. Now the array AAA becomes [2+7,1,6,3+7,5+7]=[9,1,6,10,12][2 + 7, 1, 6, 3 + 7, 5 + 7] = [9, 1, 6, 10, 12][2+7,1,6,3+7,5+7]=[9,1,6,10,12].\n\nJJ wants to maximize the value of ∑i=2N(Ai−1⊕Ai)\\displaystyle \\sum_{i = 2}^{N} (A_{i - 1} \\oplus A_{i})i=2∑N​(Ai−1​⊕Ai​). Can you help him to do so?\n\nHere, ⊕\\oplus⊕ denotes the bitwise XOR operation.\n\n&amp; &amp; kya\n&amp;\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line contains a single integer TTT — the number of test cases. Then the test cases follow.\nThe first line of each test case contains two space-separated integers NNN and XXX — the size of the array AAA and the parameter XXX mentioned in the statement.\nThe second line of each test case contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​ denoting the array AAA.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output the maximum value of ∑i=2n(Ai−1⊕Ai)\\displaystyle \\sum_{i = 2}^{n} (A_{i - 1} \\oplus A_{i})i=2∑n​(Ai−1​⊕Ai​) which can be obtained after applying the given operation **at most once**.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "1≤N≤1051 \\leq N \\leq 10^51≤N≤105",
      "1≤X≤1091 \\le X \\le 10^91≤X≤109",
      "1≤Ai≤1091 \\le A_i \\le 10^91≤Ai​≤109",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n2 1\n1 2\n4 1\n2 2 3 3\n5 2\n5 3 6 2 8",
        "output": "3\n15\n43",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: It is optimal to not perform the given operation. So the answer will equal 1⊕2=31 \\oplus 2 = 31⊕2=3.\nTest case 222: It is optimal to add X=1X = 1X=1 to the 2nd2^{nd}2nd and the 3rd3^{rd}3rd element. So AAA will become [2,3,4,3][2, 3, 4, 3][2,3,4,3] and the answer will be (2⊕3)+(3⊕4)+(4⊕3)=15(2 \\oplus 3) + (3 \\oplus 4) + (4 \\oplus 3) = 15(2⊕3)+(3⊕4)+(4⊕3)=15."
      }
    ]
  },
